  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p> </p>\n<p>Show off your healthy lifestyle while supporting NutritionFacts.org. Our limited edition <a href=\"https://www.customink.com/fundraising/nutritionfacts21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.customink.com/fundraising/nutritionfacts21\">tee and tank</a> are perfect for your summer activities, and all proceeds go to keeping NutritionFacts.org going and growing. Don’t wait to order, though. These items are only available until July 4. Get them <a href=\"https://www.customink.com/fundraising/nutritionfacts21\">here</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Key Takeaways: Thyroid Health</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/thyroid-health/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67738 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Thyroid\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Thyroid.jpg 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>A butterfly-shaped gland found low on the front of the neck, the thyroid is part of the endocrine system, which is made up of glands that produce, store, and release hormones into the bloodstream. Thyroid hormones primarily influence our metabolism, growth, development, and body temperature. I recently did a webinar on iodine and thyroid function, and those videos are now all out on NutritionFacts.org. Watch them—and learn more about thyroid health—<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/thyroid-health/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Recipe: Yellow Split Pea Dal with Watercress</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/yellow-split-pea-dal-with-watercress/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67740 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Yellow Split Pea Dal with Watercress\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Yellow-Split-Pea-Dal-with-Watercress-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Dal is a staple in Indian cuisine and packed with rich spices. This bright meal is flavored with ginger, cumin, coriander, and turmeric. It is both warm and comforting, but light enough to be enjoyed all year round. Serve it over whole grains to check off several Daily Dozen items in one meal. You can find the <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/yellow-split-pea-dal-with-watercress/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">recipe here</a>, and a video on how it’s made <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CO2_6g9JFVz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CO2_6g9JFVz/\">here</a>.</p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Welcome, Dan and Nick! </h4>\n<p>Dan and Nick recently joined our team and are responsible for day-to-day technical tasks, including development, maintenance, and administration of the NutritionFacts.org website to help bring you the latest in clinical nutrition.</p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/c1bae6687e1e6ab175fb56913/images/bcf7d6d8-9fbb-e4bf-1fc7-87aeadf34937.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" align=\"left\" data-file-id=\"6058\" data-cke-saved-src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/c1bae6687e1e6ab175fb56913/images/bcf7d6d8-9fbb-e4bf-1fc7-87aeadf34937.png\"/>Dan has degrees in computer science and completed his doctoral research on machine learning, though his career has focused on web development. He has been a plant-based eater since 2016 and can often be found in the kitchen with his daughter, proving what is good for you tastes great, too. Dan lives in northern California with his wife, daughter, and two dogs.</p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">\n</p><p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/c1bae6687e1e6ab175fb56913/images/7769f6d3-e355-5076-0f18-04873dba37c2.jpeg\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" align=\"left\" data-file-id=\"6054\" data-cke-saved-src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/c1bae6687e1e6ab175fb56913/images/7769f6d3-e355-5076-0f18-04873dba37c2.jpeg\"/>Nick is a full-stack web developer. When he’s not developing websites and web apps, he enjoys learning French, reading up on global politics, and animal rights activism. He spends most of his time between Florida and the United Kingdom.</p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Vitamin D Infographic</h4>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67734 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B-1024x1018.jpg\" alt=\"Vitamin D Infographic\" width=\"201\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B-1024x1018.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B-960x955.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B-768x764.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B-720x716.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B-540x537.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/PPC-1080x1080-B.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/>Is it necessary to take vitamin D supplements? Vitamin D is made mostly by animals, including ourselves, when we’re exposed to sunlight. Based on randomized, controlled studies, it may help us enjoy a healthier life. If you don’t get adequate sun exposure, I recommend 2,000 IU vitamin D supplements daily, ideally with the largest meal of the day. You can now get a summary of my vitamin D information in a printable, shareable infographic when you <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\">subscribe to our emails</a>. </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Meghan’s Health Story </h4>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><em><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67736 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Testimonial\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/06/Testimonial.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>I was diagnosed with stage 4 colon cancer at age 38. Genetic testing showed no predisposition, and my General Practitioner asked if that left me with more questions than answers. It did! I told her I had cut out red meat at the suggestion of my oncologist. She said, “That’s great! Keep going; in fact…cut out the white meat, dairy, and eggs.” Of course I asked, “What would I eat?!!” Then she asked me if I had heard of TMAO, and she wrote that down on a post-it, along with <a href=\"https://NutritionFacts.org/\">NutritionFacts.org</a>.</em></p><em>\n</em><p><em>Watching the <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/tmao/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">videos on TMAO</a> and other topics really helped me. I saw that if my diet could do this to me, it could fix me too! I also read Dr. Greger’s book, </em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-die/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How Not to Die</a><em>. I had phenomenal, unbelievable success by implementing the dietary changes I was originally afraid of, and I am 3 years still cancer free.</em> </p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\" data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-60211 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-healthiest-natural-source-of-iodine/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-66745\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"The Healthiest Natural Source of Iodine\" width=\"249\" height=\"140\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-24-The-Healthiest-Natural-Source-of-Iodine.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-healthiest-natural-source-of-iodine/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Healthiest Natural Source of Iodine</a></p>\n<p>How much nori, dulse, or arame approximate the recommended daily allowance for iodine?</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-hypothyroidism-and-hyperthyroidism/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-66750\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"249\" height=\"140\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-25-The-Best-Diet-for-Hypothyroidism-and-Hyperthyroidism.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-diet-for-hypothyroidism-and-hyperthyroidism/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Best Diet for Hypothyroidism and Hyperthyroidism</a></p>\n<p>Is the apparent protection of plant-based diets for thyroid health due to the exclusion of animal foods, the benefits of plant foods, or both?</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/benefits-of-black-cumin-seed-nigella-sativa-for-weight-loss/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67447\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Benefits of Black Cumin Seed (Nigella Sativa) for Weight Loss\" width=\"249\" height=\"140\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/05/54-01-Benefits-of-Black-Cumin-Seed-Nigella-Sativa-for-Weight-Loss.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/benefits-of-black-cumin-seed-nigella-sativa-for-weight-loss/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Benefits of Black Cumin Seed for Weight Loss</a></p>\n<p>For three cents a day, black cumin may improve cholesterol and triglyceride levels, blood pressure, and blood sugar control, as well as accelerate the loss of body fat.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Next Live Q&amp;A on July 22</h4>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-53879 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"Live Q&amp;A\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>My once-monthly live Q&amp;As are now going bi-monthly. Don’t worry, though. It’s only temporary while I focus my time on researching and writing my next book, <em>How Not to Age</em> (coming out in 2022). Join me for the next Q&amp;A on <em><strong>July 22</strong></em>.</p>\n<p>Join on our <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\">Facebook</a> page or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\">YouTube</a> channel at 3pm ET. I’ll be streaming to both at the same time!</p>\n<p>You can find links to past live Q&amp;As <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a> on NutritionFacts.org. If that’s not enough, don’t forget I have an <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">audio podcast</a> to keep you company, too.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
